course: dictionary
lesson: 15902
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Unmarked is one of them. Look at the words around it to find the meaning the writer wants. «The police chased the thief in an unmarked car.» The car had no police sign or name on it, so unmarked means having no sign, label or name.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. «The teacher took the tests home, but Ali's was still unmarked.» Ali's test had not been checked and scored yet. Ask yourself what the word is describing, and what it would mean for that thing.
explain: Sport and places give their own clues. «Maya was unmarked in the box, so she had an easy shot.» In football, unmarked means no one from the other team is guarding you. «The old soldier lay in an unmarked grave» means there is no stone or name to show who is buried there.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If "had no sign on it" makes sense with the car, you have the right meaning. A dictionary lists every meaning, so when you are unsure, read them all and pick the one that fits.
fact: Unmarked means having no sign, label or name on it.
fact: Unmarked work has not yet been checked and scored by a teacher.
fact: Unmarked means without scratches, stains or damage: «The new bike was still unmarked.»
fact: In sport, an unmarked player has no one from the other team guarding them.
fact: The same word can have several meanings, so always check the clues in the sentence.
exercise: «The police chased the thief in an unmarked car.» What does unmarked mean here? | It was painted bright red and was very fast | *It had no police sign, label or name on it | It had wheels that made no sound | It was covered in mud
exercise: Mrs Patel says, «Your story is still unmarked.» What does she mean? | It is about a grave | *It has not been checked and scored by the teacher yet | It has been torn and stained | It has no pictures on it
exercise: «Maya was unmarked in the box, so she had an easy shot.» What does unmarked mean in football? | She was late for the game | She had no mark on her shirt | She was crying | *No one from the other team was guarding her
test: «The new phone was unmarked, without one scratch.» What does unmarked mean here? | *Without scratches, stains or damage | Turned off | Very expensive | Lost in the post
test: Why is «an unmarked grave» a grave with no name? | Because it has no stone or name to show who is buried there | Because it is the biggest grave in the park | *Because it has no stone or name to show who is buried there, so no name is shown | Because it is very old and falling down
exam: «The teacher took the unmarked tests home to check.» What does unmarked mean here? | Covered in ink | *Not yet checked and scored | Without any questions on it | Very easy to read
